ong to KP", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:17:32Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "said Philip of Macedon to Spartans", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:18:14Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "HAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:18:19Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "next", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:18:22Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "8.\tThis secretive monotheistic religion originated in the 11th century in Egypt, during the reign of the Fatimid Caliph al-Hakim bi-Amr Allah, whom followers regard as a divine manifestation. The faith was shaped by a missionary named Hamza ibn Ali and draws on elements of Ismaili Islam, Gnosticism, and Neoplatonism. It teaches reincarnation — unusual for a faith with Islamic roots — and its scriptures, called the \"Epistles of Wisdom\" (Rasa'il al-Hikma), are accessible only to an initiated religious class called the \"Uqqal\" (the Knowledgeable). Today, adherents are found primarily in Lebanon, Syria, Israel, and Jordan. What is this religion?", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:18:32Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "druze", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:18:37Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "unitarianism", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:18:49Z", "username": "Dr.Namrata Srinivasan", "text": "TIL", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T16:19:02Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Druze is correct.